Thylacine DX-8: a system-wide base-layer config at /lib/dosbox-x/dosbox-x.conf.

Upstream DOSBox-X has no system-wide config location: on a plain launch it
searches the current directory, the executable's directory, then the per-user
XDG directory, loads the FIRST hit exclusively, and on a first launch GENERATES
the per-user file from the built-in defaults (every key written explicitly).
So a build-time default -- autolock=true, core=dynamic_rec, the cycle preset --
had nowhere to live: whatever the image wanted, the user's generated file pinned
the built-in defaults over it forever after.

This adds one Thylacine-only step at the top of the resolution: parse
/lib/dosbox-x/dosbox-x.conf (baked by tools/build.sh, SYSTEM-owned, read-only)
as a BASE LAYER, then clear the loaded-file list so the upstream flow runs
byte-for-byte as before. Consequences, in order:
  - a first launch's generated per-user config inherits the system values
    (PrintConfig writes the current values), so the user's file starts sane;
  - the per-user config, a cwd/exe-dir dosbox-x.conf, -conf files and -set
    all still override it (they are parsed later, values-last-wins);
  - -defaultconf ignores it like every other config file;
  - the line "CONFIG: Loaded system config: ..." is the gate witness.

--- a/src/gui/sdlmain.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/sdlmain.cpp
@@ -8589,6 +8589,24 @@
     bool default_config = false;
 
     struct stat st;
+
+#if defined(__thylacine__)
+    /* Thylacine: a system-wide base layer. /lib/dosbox-x/dosbox-x.conf is baked
+     * by the build (SYSTEM-owned, read-only) and parsed FIRST, so its values sit
+     * under everything the unmodified search below loads on top of them: the
+     * per-user config (which a first launch GENERATES from these values via
+     * PrintConfig), a dosbox-x.conf in the current or exe directory, -conf files,
+     * -set. Only the values carry over -- the loaded-file list is cleared so the
+     * upstream flow (probe, create-on-first-run, search, "Loaded config file")
+     * runs exactly as before. -defaultconf skips it like every other file. */
+    if (!control->opt_defaultconf) {
+        const char *sysconf = "/lib/dosbox-x/dosbox-x.conf";
+        if (control->ParseConfigFile(sysconf)) {
+            LOG_MSG("CONFIG: Loaded system config: %s", sysconf);
+            control->configfiles.clear();
+        }
+    }
+#endif
 
     control->ParseConfigFile(config_combined.c_str());
     if(!control->configfiles.size() && config_combined.size()) {
